/*
:name: arr_comb_mux_const
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: arr_comb_mux_const
:pyrope_top: arr_comb_mux_const
*/
// TRACKER — an UNDRIVEN element of an UNPACKED array is modelled as FREE rather
// than as a DON'T-CARE, so lec refutes a pair that is equivalent by intent.
//
// The golden drives only `arr[0]`; `arr[1]` has no driver, which in Verilog is
// X and means "any value is acceptable". The Pyrope side starts from
// `mut arr:[2]u1 = 0`, so its element 1 is 0. Reading `arr[sel]` at sel==1
// therefore compares a committed 0 against the golden's unknown.
//
// That comparison SHOULD be discharged: `formal.lec.gold_x` already defaults to
// `ignore` (the cvc5 analogue of yosys `miter -ignore_gold_x`), every Val
// carries an X bit-plane, and the miter masks ref-unknown bits out of the
// compare. It works for a PACKED net — an undriven bit there is read as a
// constant with literal `?` bits (`3'sb0??`), which seeds the plane, and the
// impl may drive it 0 OR 1 and still PROVE (measured both ways).
//
// The gap is the SOURCE, not the policy: an unpacked array becomes array state
// whose unwritten contents are UNCONSTRAINED, with no X plane at all. Free is
// not don't-care — a free symbol is chosen ADVERSARIALLY, so the solver picks
// exactly the value that breaks the miter (witness `o(ref=1 impl=0)` at sel==1).
// Fix = seed the X plane for undriven array state (the Memory `undef` pin /
// read-dout X plane is the existing representation), NOT to change the compare.
//
// MEASURED: adding `assign arr[1] = 1'b0;` to the golden makes this exact pair
// PROVEN, so the undriven element is the ONLY remaining difference.
// (`prp-v2prp2v-arr_comb_mux_const` passes: its original-Verilog leg never
// commits element 1 on either side.)
pub comb arr_comb_mux_const::[timecheck=false](sel:u1, d:u1) -> (o:u1) {
  mut arr:[2]u1 = 0
  arr[0] = d          // the golden's `1 ? d : ~d` — a constant condition, so `d`
  o = arr[sel]
}
